{"item_id":"E-RES-605","ledger":[{"claim_id":"Q01","category":"PROPOSED","evidence":[{"source_id":"C02","quote":"The diagnostic identifies the one recurring workflow, says honestly whether AI fits"},{"source_id":"C01","quote":"have a frequent, repeatable workflow with a measurable outcome"}],"rationale":"This is a diagnostic instruction and set of questions for the reader, not an assertion that Bareni has built or observed encoding-error detection anywhere. Framing an abstract topic as one recurring workflow with a frequency question is consistent with the approved diagnostic model.","use_guidance":"Keep as an explicitly proposed diagnostic question in plain English; do not imply Bareni has already inspected any customer's tools or found such errors."},{"claim_id":"Q02","category":"PROPOSED","evidence":[{"source_id":"C01","quote":"The representative pains are 8–10 hours a week of repeated customer questions, neglected sales leads,
  and manual invoice/data work"},{"source_id":"C02","quote":"defines pilot scope, fixed price, and measures"}],"rationale":"An instruction to the owner to describe and time their existing manual detection and correction practice. It asks the owner to produce their own figure rather than asserting any Bareni-supplied number or observed result.","use_guidance":"Keep as a proposed baseline-measurement step; the owner supplies the hours. Do not import the 8–10 hours persona scenario or any other figure as a measured or typical result."},{"claim_id":"Q03","category":"PROPOSED","evidence":[{"source_id":"C04","quote":"Human approval is mandatory for money movement and other high-risk decisions."},{"source_id":"C03","quote":"amount-based human-only approval,
  refusal of agent approval/payment attempts, and persistent audit records work"}],"rationale":"A mapping exercise plus a control-design step. Locating the human approval point is a permissible recommendation aligned with the mandatory human-approval boundary, not a claim about an existing implemented data-flow tool.","use_guidance":"Keep proposed; state that human approval is required before money movement or other high-risk downstream action, and do not present any encoding data-flow mapping tool as existing software."},{"claim_id":"Q04","category":"PROPOSED","evidence":[{"source_id":"C04","quote":"Bareni currently declines high-sensitivity medical, legal, and financial work;
  bulk cold-email automation; scan-heavy OCR-dependent workflows"},{"source_id":"C02","quote":"says honestly whether AI fits"}],"rationale":"A fit-assessment instruction with named exclusion checks. It recommends a test rather than asserting that Bareni has implemented charset detection or UTF-8 normalisation.","use_guidance":"Keep proposed. Also flag scan-heavy/OCR-dependent variants as currently out of scope, and present these boundaries as current scope discipline rather than a permanent technical limit. Do not imply working OCR or PDF/scan ingestion."},{"claim_id":"Q05","category":"QUALIFICATIONS","evidence":[{"source_id":"C02","quote":"free one-page pilot proposal;
  paid working MVP in days; fixed-price pilot in weeks"},{"source_id":"C02","quote":"Timings are intended scopes, not guarantees."},{"source_id":"C05","quote":"Never invent a benchmark, guarantee, ROI,
  saving, revenue lift, productivity result"}],"rationale":"The one-page proposal, bounded MVP, fixed price, human review flag and pilot-in-weeks sequence are supported, but the claim states a definite "two-week delivery window" without the required intended-scope caveat, and "reduction in manual correction time" as a success measure needs the owner's own baseline rather than any promised saving.","use_guidance":"Add the qualification that pilot timing is an intended scope, not a guarantee, and that the success measure is a target agreed against the owner's own baseline, not a promised or observed reduction. Keep the pilot itself explicitly as a proposal; a paid working MVP in days may precede the fixed-price pilot."},{"claim_id":"Q06","category":"FORBIDDEN","evidence":[{"source_id":"S01","quote":"**CTA rule:** None."},{"source_id":"C05","quote":"Use it only for
  purchase-intent content, once, at the end."}],"rationale":"The approved task explicitly authorises no CTA, so inviting the reader to book a free 30-minute diagnostic is a prohibited action for this item, even though the diagnostic itself exists as a service.","use_guidance":"Exclude the invitation and any booking CTA. If a closing line is needed, use at most one soft informational sentence about examining one recent encoding incident. The existence of a free 30-minute diagnostic is separately supported by C02, but that does not approve using it as a CTA here."}]}

